een references, in their exact order.\n- The official cartoon girl reference image.\n- Benny's 3D GLB model, source code, textures, and animations.\n- The cartoon girl's GLB model, source code, textures, and animations.\n- All washing-machine environment geometry.\n- All metallic tunnels, gold rings, washer interiors, and machinery.\n- All animated cyan-and-pink water systems.\n- Foam, bubbles, splashes, shaders, and lighting.\n- Gameplay path, swimming movement, camera, controls, coins, hearts, and HUD.\n- The Android Capacitor application and available APK.\n- All Playwright screenshots, reference comparisons, and visual QA tests.\n- All saved Blender scripts and available 3D source files.\n- The World Labs Screen 05 pilot package.\n- All prompts, reference-matching instructions, recovery documents, and project history.\n- The previous Claude conversation transcripts and specialist logs that are actually stored in GitHub.\n- The automatic backup scripts, configuration files, and session hooks.\n\nRun \"git lfs pull\" after cloning or fetching the project so the real models and other large files are restored rather than leaving only Git LFS pointer files.\n\nVerify the actual contents and integrity of important binary assets.\n\nDo not assume a file is restored merely because its filename exists.\n\n3. RESTORE ALL TEN SPECIALIST DESIGN AGENTS\n\nMy project already has ten specialist agents saved in:\n\n\".claude/agents/\"\n\nRestore and verify every one:\n\n1. Reference Match Director\n2. Benny Character Artist\n3. Cartoon Girl Character Artist\n4. Washer Environment Modeler\n5. Water FX Specialist\n6. Foam and Bubble Specialist\n7. Path and Camera Transition Engineer\n8. Animation and Gameplay Engineer\n9. Playwright Visual QA Specialist\n10. Android Build and Performance Specialist\n\nDo not create new replacement agents if my existing ones are recoverable.\n\nRead their actual saved instructions, responsibilities, work logs, and latest completed tasks.\n\nRestore their project context and reinitialize the agents needed for the unfinished work.\n\nI understand that live agent processes cannot simply be transferred between Claude accounts. Restart the specialists from their saved configurations, previous outputs, and progress notes.\n\nPreserve their completed work.\n\nCoordinate the specialists so they can improve the game together instead of duplicating or overwriting one another's work.\n\n4. RESTORE ALL DEVELOPMENT TOOLS, SERVERS, AND PLUGINS\n\nInspect the saved project configuration and recover or reconnect the supported tools.\n\nBLENDER\n\nMy previous environment used Blender 5.3.0.\n\nVerify whether Blender is available in this new Claude environment.\n\nUse Blender Python scripting for automated 3D modeling and rendering.\n\nIf Blender MCP is available and working, use it where appropriate.\n\nIf the desktop Blender MCP requires a graphical window unavailable in this cloud environment, continue with headless Blender and Python scripts instead.\n\nDo not falsely report Blender MCP as connected if it is not.\n\nUse Blender to improve the washer geometry, tunnel shapes, metallic materials, character models, and visual accuracy.\n\nWORLD LABS MARBLE / ATLAS\n\nRestore the existing official World Labs plugin and its available MCP configuration.\n\nMy previous Claude environment had the official World Labs plugin installed and an Atlas connector configured.\n\nVerify whether World Labs authentication is available in this new account.\n\nIf my Atlas account has not been activated, report the account-access problem and continue with the other available tools.\n\nDo not demand an API key if a supported OAuth sign-in can be used.\n\nUse World Labs to help reconstruct my exact approved Rainbow environments when the account and tools are ready.\n\nDo not generate unrelated or redesigned environments.\n\nDo not spend paid World Labs credits until I explicitly approve the cost.\n\nPLAYWRIGHT\n\nRestore Playwright and the mobile 